    12	# Design analysis for the fused variant
    13	# a) Concrete behavior trace:
    14	#    Original e12f9a14 launches straight diagonal/cardinal beams from frame gaps and spends most
    15	#    of its logic on beam/beam collisions. This combo replaces the motion itself. Example:
    16	#    for a top-side gap, the original would shoot outward in one fixed direction; here the gap
    17	#    first paints itself, steps one cell outward, then grows a clockwise self-avoiding spiral.
    18	#    The hidden spiral path is continuous, but the visible paint is distance-banded:
    19	#    the first few cells are solid, the next band paints every other step, then every third step,
    20	#    etc. The visible difference is therefore twofold: many right-angle turns, and increasing gaps
    21	#    on outer rings.
    22	# b) Complexity calibration:
    23	#    To keep the rule legible in 2-4 examples, the generator only uses side gaps, not corner gaps.
    24	#    That keeps the launch heading cardinal, so the spiral direction is easy to read by eye.
    25	#    Multiple framed blocks still appear, but each frame emits exactly one spiral; this preserves
    26	#    repetition without turning the output into an unreadable mesh.
    27	# c) Hidden-assumption audit:
    28	#    The original solver assumed gaps could launch collision-capable beams in any of the 8 outward
    29	#    directions, and that later state depended on beam interactions. None of those assumptions hold
    30	#    after switching to independent spirals. The new solver assumes:
    31	#    - every generated launch gap is on a side cell of the 4x4 frame, so the outward heading is
    32	#      cardinal;
    33	#    - spirals are solved independently, with no hidden inter-spiral collision rules;
    34	#    - self-avoidance matters for the full hidden path, while the visible sparse paint is derived
    35	#      afterward from that path.
    36	#    The generator explicitly enforces all of these assumptions.
    37	# d) Placement legality:
    38	#    Frames are placed with generous clearance, and the generator pre-traces every candidate spiral
    39	#    on the obstacle grid before committing to a gap. It rejects short traces, low-turn traces, and
    40	#    any pair of traces whose full paths overlap or touch orthogonally.
    41	# e) Visual observability / cleanliness / inferability:
    42	#    The human-visible signal is structural, not color-id based: each output trail still uses the
